WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:02.300
As soon as it happened the media...

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:03.770
Oh, it's because of the music.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.710
Today, rap music has come under fire in some

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.470
quarters. Run DMC says it preaches positive

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:11.900
messages, yet its tour has been marred by

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.790
violence. Today, the group held a news

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.680
conference to say none of this was its

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:16.190
fault.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.680
We don't think our music and concert inspires

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.000
this kind of behavior.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.980
Stuff like this been happening since the

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:22.970
dawn of time.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.840
Listen to run DMC, you won't find nothing

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.680
that incites or promotes what happened at

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.030
the L.A. Coliseum.

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.040
We were trying to introduce to hip hop

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.650
culture that could save and transform your

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.380
communities and your individual being.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.060
L.A. wasn't ready for that sh*t.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.120
At that time, I sniffed.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.640
That there was a seat change.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.060
So NWA was our opening act and they were

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.170
bringing the heat.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.440
That heat was hot.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.270
And I walked in to our dressing room and

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.350
said, "Houston,

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:12.600
we have a problem." What's cracking.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.640
It's your homeboy, Ice cube.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:16.950
West coast warlord.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:18.840
Grand wizard.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.400
Self-made. Cool-Aid.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.980
My first record I ever bought with my own

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.490
money was the first Run-DMC album.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.980
I think the record cost $7.99, and I had

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:40.970
about $3 $4 and my man had about $4, and we

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:42.170
bought the album.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.840
It would be at my house for four days and at

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.190
his house for three days.

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:49.670
I'm telling you, like clockwork, when it was

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:52.040
my turn. Boom boom boom boom.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.600
Give me the record, man.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.980
To me, run was the dopest MC on the planet.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:01:59.990
It's like Run D.M.C.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.520
saying, what the hell they want to say.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.580
Why we can't. And so when it was our turn,

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.470
we did what we was supposed to do.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:11.760
We gave him the blueprint attitude, how to

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.040
rock those mics and make those beats.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:20.070
Then they started taking specific aspects of

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:25.920
socio economical, cultural, political trauma

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:31.650
and addressed it in a way that was bold

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:32.310
faced.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.550
When I started to get into rap, I wanted to

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:36.990
rap like Run-DMC.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.480
I wanted to rap like New York rappers.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:43.170
My boys were saying, say that other sh*t

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.660
talking about these criminal rhymes that I

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.420
would say. It was like, oh, y'all want to

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:51.420
hear this sh*t? This is what I do.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.820
Press said, it's gangster rap.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.420
Gangsta rap, the rap style of a ghetto world

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.010
where everybody's got a gun.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:01.650
Women are b*tches and shooting cops is fair

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:02.400
game.

